-- ## The derived and replacement rules: `forallx-magnus-plus`
--
-- Everything above this line is `forallx-magnus.mm0`, verbatim. This
-- artifact — served at `/theories/forallx-magnus-plus.mm0`, named by
-- `system="forallx-magnus-plus"` — is that file with the rules the book's
-- chapter on derived rules adds: dilemma, modus tollens and hypothetical
-- syllogism, the five rules of replacement for SL, and quantifier negation
-- for QL. Two systems on purpose, for the reason `forallx-calgary-2019-plus`
-- gives: every rule here is a theorem of the basic set, and which set a
-- proof may cite is the course's call. Old Carnap draws the same line
-- (`magnusQL` against `magnusQLPlus`), and the citation names are its.
--
-- **The replacement rules rewrite inside a sentence**, as the book's do:
-- `Comm`, `DN`, `MC`, `↔ex`, `DeM` and `QN` take a line to the same line with
-- one subsentence exchanged for its equivalent, wherever that subsentence
-- sits — `¬¬P → Q` to `P → Q` in one step. Each is an axiom over a *context*:
-- `r` is the line's sentence with a hole `h` where the exchange happens, and
-- `sbw φ h r` plugs φ into the hole. The `@abstract` line finds the hole. It
-- walks the cited sentence and the new one together, and at the outermost
-- position where they differ tries the two patterns — the rule's left and
-- right sides — solving their variables from what it finds; the rest of the
-- sentence, identical on both sides, becomes `r`. The `@rewrite` equations
-- push `sbw` back through the connectives so the normalizer can check that
-- the plugged context is the line as written. The sites the line changes
-- are rewritten at once, one substitution serving all of them; two sites
-- that would need different substitutions are refused, and so is a line
-- that changes anything outside the exchange.
--
-- The hole `h` is a bound `wff` variable the engine invents (`@fresh h`
-- draws on `wff`'s `@vars` pool, the single token `_0` declared above). A
-- pool token is a name the surface language reads, so it is spelled so
-- that a student cannot use it by accident: letter-free, because every
-- letter is a delimiter here and would split anything else, and refused
-- in a proof line by the closed-sentences lint, which sees a free
-- variable. `_0` is the only token, and one is enough — a hole is bound
-- per rule application, not consumed.
--
-- ## forallx rule → axiom name
--
--   DIL ... dil            MT ... mt            HS ... hs
--   Comm .. and_comm / or_comm / iff_comm
--   DN .... dn_elim / dn_intro
--   MC .... mc_imp_or / mc_or_imp / mc_or_negimp / mc_negimp_or
--   ↔ex ... iffex_split / iffex_join
--   DeM ... dem_neg_or / dem_and_neg / dem_neg_and / dem_or_neg
--   QN .... qn_neg_all / qn_ex_neg / qn_neg_ex / qn_all_neg
--
-- Where a name covers several rules — every replacement rule but `Comm` runs
-- in both directions, and `Comm` over three connectives — the alias sits on
-- the last axiom, which `@fallback`s onto the ones before it in turn, exactly
-- as `&E` does above: a line citing `DeM` gets whichever form fits, and the
-- certificate names the one that held. `Comm` needs no second direction: its
-- two sides are each other's instances.

-- Dilemma: proof by cases with the cases already conditionalized.
--| @syntax alias DIL
axiom dil (ga de si ta: ctx) (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ga ⊢ ph ∨ ps $ > $ de ⊢ ph → ch $ > $ si ⊢ ps → ch $ >
  $ ga ; de ; si ; ta ⊢ ch $;

-- Modus tollens
--| @syntax alias MT
axiom mt (ga de si: ctx) (ph ps: wff):
  $ ga ⊢ ph → ps $ > $ de ⊢ ¬ ps $ > $ ga ; de ; si ⊢ ¬ ph $;

-- Hypothetical syllogism
--| @syntax alias HS
axiom hs (ga de si: ctx) (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ga ⊢ ph → ps $ > $ de ⊢ ps → ch $ > $ ga ; de ; si ⊢ ph → ch $;

-- The hole, and substitution into it. `sbw th h r` is r with th at every
-- occurrence of h; the equations push it through the syntax to the hole
-- (`sbw_var`) or to a subsentence with no hole in it (`sbw_vac`). Atomic
-- sentences contain no sentence, so `sbw_vac` is all they need.
term sbw (th: wff) {h: wff} (ph: wff h): wff;
--| @rewrite
axiom sbw_var (th: wff) {h: wff}: $ sbw th h h ⟺ th $;
--| @rewrite
axiom sbw_vac (th: wff) {h: wff} (ph: wff): $ sbw th h ph ⟺ ph $;
--| @rewrite
axiom sbw_not (th: wff) {h: wff} (ph: wff h):
  $ sbw th h (¬ ph) ⟺ ¬ (sbw th h ph) $;
--| @rewrite
axiom sbw_and (th: wff) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff h):
  $ sbw th h (ph ∧ ps) ⟺ (sbw th h ph ∧ sbw th h ps) $;
--| @rewrite
axiom sbw_or (th: wff) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff h):
  $ sbw th h (ph ∨ ps) ⟺ (sbw th h ph ∨ sbw th h ps) $;
--| @rewrite
axiom sbw_imp (th: wff) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff h):
  $ sbw th h (ph → ps) ⟺ (sbw th h ph → sbw th h ps) $;
--| @rewrite
axiom sbw_iff (th: wff) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff h):
  $ sbw th h (ph ↔ ps) ⟺ (sbw th h ph ↔ sbw th h ps) $;
--| @rewrite
axiom sbw_all {h: wff} {x: var} (th: wff x) (ph: wff h x):
  $ sbw th h (∀ x ph) ⟺ ∀ x (sbw th h ph) $;
--| @rewrite
axiom sbw_ex {h: wff} {x: var} (th: wff x) (ph: wff h x):
  $ sbw th h (∃ x ph) ⟺ ∃ x (sbw th h ph) $;

-- Commutativity, of each of the three commutative connectives.
--| @view (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h) (p q: wff): $ ga ⊢ p $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ q $
--| @abstract r p q h $ ph ∧ ps $ $ ps ∧ ph $
--| @fresh h
axiom and_comm (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h):
  $ ga ⊢ sbw (ph ∧ ps) h r $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ sbw (ps ∧ ph) h r $;
--| @view (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h) (p q: wff): $ ga ⊢ p $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ q $
--| @abstract r p q h $ ph ∨ ps $ $ ps ∨ ph $
--| @fresh h
--| @fallback and_comm
axiom or_comm (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h):
  $ ga ⊢ sbw (ph ∨ ps) h r $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ sbw (ps ∨ ph) h r $;
--| @view (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h) (p q: wff): $ ga ⊢ p $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ q $
--| @abstract r p q h $ ph ↔ ps $ $ ps ↔ ph $
--| @fresh h
--| @fallback or_comm
--| @syntax alias Comm
axiom iff_comm (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h):
  $ ga ⊢ sbw (ph ↔ ps) h r $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ sbw (ps ↔ ph) h r $;

-- Double negation, both ways.
--| @view (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph: wff) (r: wff h) (p q: wff): $ ga ⊢ p $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ q $
--| @abstract r p q h $ ¬ ¬ ph $ $ ph $
--| @fresh h
axiom dn_elim (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph: wff) (r: wff h):
  $ ga ⊢ sbw (¬ ¬ ph) h r $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ sbw ph h r $;
--| @view (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph: wff) (r: wff h) (p q: wff): $ ga ⊢ p $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ q $
--| @abstract r p q h $ ph $ $ ¬ ¬ ph $
--| @fresh h
--| @fallback dn_elim
--| @syntax alias DN
axiom dn_intro (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph: wff) (r: wff h):
  $ ga ⊢ sbw ph h r $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ sbw (¬ ¬ ph) h r $;

-- Material conditional: a conditional as a disjunction and a disjunction as
-- a conditional, each both ways.
--| @view (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h) (p q: wff): $ ga ⊢ p $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ q $
--| @abstract r p q h $ ph → ps $ $ ¬ ph ∨ ps $
--| @fresh h
axiom mc_imp_or (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h):
  $ ga ⊢ sbw (ph → ps) h r $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ sbw (¬ ph ∨ ps) h r $;
--| @view (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h) (p q: wff): $ ga ⊢ p $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ q $
--| @abstract r p q h $ ¬ ph ∨ ps $ $ ph → ps $
--| @fresh h
--| @fallback mc_imp_or
axiom mc_or_imp (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h):
  $ ga ⊢ sbw (¬ ph ∨ ps) h r $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ sbw (ph → ps) h r $;
--| @view (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h) (p q: wff): $ ga ⊢ p $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ q $
--| @abstract r p q h $ ph ∨ ps $ $ ¬ ph → ps $
--| @fresh h
--| @fallback mc_or_imp
axiom mc_or_negimp (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h):
  $ ga ⊢ sbw (ph ∨ ps) h r $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ sbw (¬ ph → ps) h r $;
--| @view (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h) (p q: wff): $ ga ⊢ p $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ q $
--| @abstract r p q h $ ¬ ph → ps $ $ ph ∨ ps $
--| @fresh h
--| @fallback mc_or_negimp
--| @syntax alias MC
axiom mc_negimp_or (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h):
  $ ga ⊢ sbw (¬ ph → ps) h r $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ sbw (ph ∨ ps) h r $;

-- Biconditional exchange: a biconditional as the conjunction of its two
-- conditionals, both ways.
--| @view (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h) (p q: wff): $ ga ⊢ p $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ q $
--| @abstract r p q h $ ph ↔ ps $ $ (ph → ps) ∧ (ps → ph) $
--| @fresh h
axiom iffex_split (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h):
  $ ga ⊢ sbw (ph ↔ ps) h r $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ sbw ((ph → ps) ∧ (ps → ph)) h r $;
--| @view (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h) (p q: wff): $ ga ⊢ p $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ q $
--| @abstract r p q h $ (ph → ps) ∧ (ps → ph) $ $ ph ↔ ps $
--| @fresh h
--| @fallback iffex_split
--| @syntax alias ↔ex <->ex
axiom iffex_join (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h):
  $ ga ⊢ sbw ((ph → ps) ∧ (ps → ph)) h r $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ sbw (ph ↔ ps) h r $;

-- De Morgan, the four forms.
--| @view (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h) (p q: wff): $ ga ⊢ p $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ q $
--| @abstract r p q h $ ¬ (ph ∨ ps) $ $ ¬ ph ∧ ¬ ps $
--| @fresh h
axiom dem_neg_or (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h):
  $ ga ⊢ sbw (¬ (ph ∨ ps)) h r $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ sbw (¬ ph ∧ ¬ ps) h r $;
--| @view (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h) (p q: wff): $ ga ⊢ p $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ q $
--| @abstract r p q h $ ¬ ph ∧ ¬ ps $ $ ¬ (ph ∨ ps) $
--| @fresh h
--| @fallback dem_neg_or
axiom dem_and_neg (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h):
  $ ga ⊢ sbw (¬ ph ∧ ¬ ps) h r $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ sbw (¬ (ph ∨ ps)) h r $;
--| @view (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h) (p q: wff): $ ga ⊢ p $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ q $
--| @abstract r p q h $ ¬ (ph ∧ ps) $ $ ¬ ph ∨ ¬ ps $
--| @fresh h
--| @fallback dem_and_neg
axiom dem_neg_and (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h):
  $ ga ⊢ sbw (¬ (ph ∧ ps)) h r $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ sbw (¬ ph ∨ ¬ ps) h r $;
--| @view (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h) (p q: wff): $ ga ⊢ p $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ q $
--| @abstract r p q h $ ¬ ph ∨ ¬ ps $ $ ¬ (ph ∧ ps) $
--| @fresh h
--| @fallback dem_neg_and
--| @syntax alias DeM
axiom dem_or_neg (ga de: ctx) {h: wff} (ph ps: wff) (r: wff h):
  $ ga ⊢ sbw (¬ ph ∨ ¬ ps) h r $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ sbw (¬ (ph ∧ ps)) h r $;

-- Quantifier negation, the four forms. The exchanged subsentence binds a
-- variable, so the pattern does too, and the context and the line may
-- mention it outside the site, as the quantifier rules above allow.
--| @view {h: wff} {x: var} (ga de: ctx x) (ph: wff x) (r: wff h x) (p q: wff x): $ ga ⊢ p $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ q $
--| @abstract r p q h $ ¬ (∀ x ph) $ $ ∃ x (¬ ph) $
--| @fresh h
axiom qn_neg_all {h: wff} {x: var} (ga de: ctx x) (ph: wff x) (r: wff h x):
  $ ga ⊢ sbw (¬ (∀ x ph)) h r $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ sbw (∃ x (¬ ph)) h r $;
--| @view {h: wff} {x: var} (ga de: ctx x) (ph: wff x) (r: wff h x) (p q: wff x): $ ga ⊢ p $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ q $
--| @abstract r p q h $ ∃ x (¬ ph) $ $ ¬ (∀ x ph) $
--| @fresh h
--| @fallback qn_neg_all
axiom qn_ex_neg {h: wff} {x: var} (ga de: ctx x) (ph: wff x) (r: wff h x):
  $ ga ⊢ sbw (∃ x (¬ ph)) h r $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ sbw (¬ (∀ x ph)) h r $;
--| @view {h: wff} {x: var} (ga de: ctx x) (ph: wff x) (r: wff h x) (p q: wff x): $ ga ⊢ p $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ q $
--| @abstract r p q h $ ¬ (∃ x ph) $ $ ∀ x (¬ ph) $
--| @fresh h
--| @fallback qn_ex_neg
axiom qn_neg_ex {h: wff} {x: var} (ga de: ctx x) (ph: wff x) (r: wff h x):
  $ ga ⊢ sbw (¬ (∃ x ph)) h r $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ sbw (∀ x (¬ ph)) h r $;
--| @view {h: wff} {x: var} (ga de: ctx x) (ph: wff x) (r: wff h x) (p q: wff x): $ ga ⊢ p $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ q $
--| @abstract r p q h $ ∀ x (¬ ph) $ $ ¬ (∃ x ph) $
--| @fresh h
--| @fallback qn_neg_ex
--| @syntax alias QN
axiom qn_all_neg {h: wff} {x: var} (ga de: ctx x) (ph: wff x) (r: wff h x):
  $ ga ⊢ sbw (∀ x (¬ ph)) h r $ > $ ga ; de ⊢ sbw (¬ (∃ x ph)) h r $;
